          "annotations": [],
          "text": "{\"stories\":[{\"id\":\"s000029\",\"rating\":{\"coherence\":6,\"style\":6,\"grammar\":8,\"storytelling\":7,\"overall\":7},\"note\":\"A clear pepper-and-berry tasting arc ends in a vivid pawprint image, though the repeated label discovery and flavor announcements make the middle redundant.\"},{\"id\":\"s000057\",\"rating\":{\"coherence\":6,\"style\":6,\"grammar\":8,\"storytelling\":6,\"overall\":6},\"note\":\"The shared-treat ending is warm and concrete, but Pip's cinnamon label is introduced without a clear correction and the flavor-label logic is muddled.\"},{\"id\":\"s000047\",\"rating\":{\"coherence\":7,\"style\":6,\"grammar\":8,\"storytelling\":6,\"overall\":7},\"note\":\"A simple decision to share leads smoothly to jam-topped bites and a pleasing crumb image, but there is little problem or consequential turn beyond sharing.\"},{\"id\":\"s000073\",\"rating\":{\"coherence\":7,\"style\":6,\"grammar\":8,\"storytelling\":6,\"overall\":7},\"note\":\"This is coherent, child-friendly prose with a concrete shared-snack conclusion, although it lacks a developed obstacle or surprise.\"},{\"id\":\"s000034\",\"rating\":{\"coherence\":7,\"style\":6,\"grammar\":8,\"storytelling\":7,\"overall\":7},\"note\":\"The confirmed cinnamon flavor supports a fair exchange and sweet tasting payoff; the ending image of Pip parading a paper sash completes the small story neatly.\"},{\"id\":\"s000043\",\"rating\":{\"coherence\":5,\"style\":6,\"grammar\":8,\"storytelling\":6,\"overall\":6},\"note\":\"The choice to share gives the scene a modest arc, but Pip calls his pepper label a 'cinnamon word,' creating an unexplained contradiction.\"},{\"id\":\"s000068\",\"rating\":{\"coherence\":7,\"style\":6,\"grammar\":8,\"storytelling\":7,\"overall\":7},\"note\":\"A mismatched pepper label is discovered before the cinnamon pastry is traded and enjoyed, producing a complete, concrete resolution despite some repeated exposition.\"},{\"id\":\"s000096\",\"rating\":{\"coherence\":5,\"style\":6,\"grammar\":8,\"storytelling\":7,\"overall\":6},\"note\":\"The daring pepper-and-berry tasting has a clear payoff and strong final image, but Pip first pins 'cinnamon' and then declares he has pinned a pepper label, confusing the central setup.\"},{\"id\":\"s000005\",\"rating\":{\"coherence\":7,\"style\":6,\"grammar\":8,\"storytelling\":7,\"overall\":7},\"note\":\"The incorrect pepper label is corrected by discovering cinnamon, and the trade ends with a clear happy bite and Pip's slipping paper sash.\"},{\"id\":\"s000085\",\"rating\":{\"coherence\":5,\"style\":6,\"grammar\":8,\"storytelling\":7,\"overall\":6},\"note\":\"The pepper-and-berry surprise and pawprint ending work well, but an extra, unexplained 'Berry jam!' decision and repeated discovery dialogue make the sequence cluttered.\"}],\"diversity\":{\"premise\":2,\"causal_path\":3,\"ending\":3,\"language\":3,\"overall\":3},\"diversity_evidence\":\"All stories use the same bakery trio, labeled button pastry, berry jam, and tasting setup. The main material branch is trade after a cinnamon/pepper-label mismatch (s000034, s000068, s000005) versus sharing the snack (s000047, s000073, s000057, s000043), while s000029, s000096, and s000085 resolve with a pepper-and-berry surprise. Most wording, scenes, and final crumb/pawprint or sash images are closely repeated; this sample does not establish diversity for the full generator.\",\"plot_groups\":[{\"story_ids\":[\"s000034\",\"s000068\",\"s000005\"],\"summary\":\"Pip's label conflicts with the cinnamon pastry; the flavor is checked, then Ada trades the button to Nia for jam, and Nia enjoys the sweet combination.\"},{\"story_ids\":[\"s000047\",\"s000073\",\"s000057\",\"s000043\"],\"summary\":\"Ada declines a trade and divides the button among the trio, who eat jam-topped pieces together.\"},{\"story_ids\":[\"s000029\",\"s000096\",\"s000085\"],\"summary\":\"A pepper button is paired with berry jam for a daring taste; Nia likes the surprising combination and the trio celebrates.\"}]}",
